<worksheet >
    <title>MD-1 Matrix Operations</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete all four parts. 
      Complete any three parts to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
   <page>
    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
        <introduction> <p>Given the following matrices:
        <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="3">
          <mrow>E=\begin{bmatrix} 2 &amp; 3 \\ 4 &amp; 1 \end{bmatrix}, 
            F=\begin{bmatrix} 0 &amp; -2 \\ 5 &amp; 1 \end{bmatrix}, 
            G=\begin{bmatrix} -1 &amp; 3 &amp; 2 \\ 4 &amp; 0 &amp; -1 \end{bmatrix}, 
            H=\begin{bmatrix} 5 &amp; 2 \\ 3 &amp; 4 \end{bmatrix}</mrow></md>
            Compute the following matrices, if possible.  If the computation is not 
            possible, explain why.</p></introduction>
    <task><statement><p><m>EF - H</m></p></statement> </task>
    <task><statement><p><m>3E^2 + 2F</m></p></statement></task>
    <task><statement><p><m>G^T H</m></p></statement></task>
    <task><statement><p><m>F + G</m></p></statement></task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>